  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1020 PM MST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nFRIDAY:\n\nHigh clouds are blanketing the area ahead of a weak shortwave\ntrough that will move through the area Friday afternoon. As this\nshortwave moves through, forcing is very limited so we could see\nsome isolated showers popping over the higher terrain with light\nsnow at the highest elevations. Very little in the way of\naccumulation is expected. Cloud cover could keep overnight lows\na bit moderated and preclude the notion of any fog development.\nSkies look to clear pretty quickly behind this shortwave Friday\nevening with an expansive ridge of high pressure moving in from\nthe west. \n\nDRIER AND MILDER THIS WEEKEND INTO THE COMING WEEK:\n\nDry and milder weather will be the rule this coming weekend \nwhich is a welcome change from the previous few weekends and \ngive us a break from the recent abundant precipitation. Looking \nahead, some systems move into the Pacific Northwest but this \nhigh pressure ridge looks to keep the storm track well north, \nallowing for dry conditions this coming week and temperatures \nwarming slightly but ending up around 5 degrees or so above \nseasonal norms.",
